    {
      "id": "mmrbpdPkR3VJrm1baFr5f",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 899.7735394328545,
      "y": 2528.0882353089587,
      "width": 1161.63916015625,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1884856363,
      "version": 378,
      "versionNonce": 896888715,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "ePacPHoRbjkorNTEbvL5E",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1788521626438,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why Inngest & Agent-kit?\n \nDirect AI requests can cause server timeouts due to slow multi-step processing. \nUsing Inngest background jobs with @inngest/agent-kit offloads execution safely,\nallowing the AI to handle complex workflows asynchronously without blocking the main HTTP server\nthrough the following core concepts:\n\nTools: \nCustom JavaScript/TypeScript functions exposed to the LLM, allowing it to perform concrete actions \n(e.g., database queries, code generation) beyond just text responses.\n\nMCP (Model Context Protocol): \nA standardized, \"USB-like\" protocol enabling seamless and secure integration between LLMs and external data sources \nor local file systems.\n\nAgents and State: \nLLM instances combined with specific prompts and tools, managed via a typed state machine \nto maintain conversation memory and context across background steps.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Inngest & Agent-kit?\n \nDirect AI requests can cause server timeouts due to slow multi-step processing. \nUsing Inngest background jobs with @inngest/agent-kit offloads execution safely,\nallowing the AI to handle complex workflows asynchronously without blocking the main HTTP server\nthrough the following core concepts:\n\nTools: \nCustom JavaScript/TypeScript functions exposed to the LLM, allowing it to perform concrete actions \n(e.g., database queries, code generation) beyond just text responses.\n\nMCP (Model Context Protocol): \nA standardized, \"USB-like\" protocol enabling seamless and secure integration between LLMs and external data sources \nor local file systems.\n\nAgents and State: \nLLM instances combined with specific prompts and tools, managed via a typed state machine \nto maintain conversation memory and context across background steps.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
